<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.head(
      title: "Get started — CSuiteFinder",
      description: "Paste one line into your assistant. It reads llms.txt, runs the demo, and hands back a CSV of verified work emails.",
      nav: :start,
      audience: :developer,
      css: CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.page_css(:start)
    ) %>

<header>
  <span class="timing">About a minute</span>
  <h1>Paste one line. Get a CSV back.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    You do not have to read our documentation, and neither do you have to write
    any code. If you use an AI assistant, one line tells it everything — every
    endpoint, every parameter, every price — and it takes over from there.
  </p>
</header>

<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Paste the line</strong><span>Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot — anything that reads a page and makes a request.</span></li>
  <li><strong>It reads <code>llms.txt</code></strong><span>Generated from the live service, so what it reads is what you are charged.</span></li>
  <li><strong>Ask for what you want</strong><span>In plain English. It knows which calls to chain.</span></li>
</ol>

<%!-- The whole page is this conversation. Rendered as markup rather than a
      screenshot so it stays readable, recolours in dark mode, and cannot go
      stale against the line above it — the paste block and the first bubble are
      the same string. --%>
<h2 class="section-label">What that looks like</h2>

<div class="chat" role="img" aria-label="A conversation with an assistant: the visitor pastes the setup line, the assistant reads llms.txt, runs the demo and returns a CSV of verified work emails.">
  <div class="turn you">
    <span class="who">You</span>
    <div class="bubble" data-signed="out">
      Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my
      token <code>csf_live_...</code> to be used. Then run /demo
    </div>
    <div class="bubble" data-signed="in" hidden>
      Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my
      token <code data-key>CSF_KEY_HERE</code> to be used. Then run /demo
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="turn bot">
    <span class="who">Assistant</span>
    <div class="bubble">
      <p>Reading <code>llms.txt</code> — 18 endpoints, prices included. Token stored.</p>

      <div class="run">
        <span class="tick">✓</span>
        <code>GET /email/company/people?domain=stripe.com&amp;department=executive&amp;limit=20</code>
        <span class="cost">$0.05</span>
      </div>
      <div class="run">
        <span class="tick">✓</span>
        <code>POST /email/deliverable</code> <span class="muted-inline">× 20</span>
        <span class="cost">included</span>
      </div>

      <p class="settle">
        20 rows, 18 deliverable, 2 undeliverable — caught before you sent to them.
        Spent <strong>$0.05</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="file">
        <span class="file-icon" aria-hidden="true">▦</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Prospects.csv</strong>
          <span>20 rows · name, title, email, deliverable</span>
        </div>
        <span class="file-done">ready</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="chat-note">
  Real shape, real prices. The sheet below is real output — same columns, run on
  <%= @sheet_date %>.
</p>

<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.sheet(
      rows: @sheet,
      rows_label: @sheet_rows,
      date: @sheet_date,
      visitor: @visitor
    ) %>

<h2 class="section-label">The line</h2>

<div class="copyblock" data-signed="out">
  <button class="copybtn" data-copy="prompt1">Copy</button>
  <pre><code id="prompt1">Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my token `csf_live_...` to be used. Then run /demo</code></pre>
</div>
<p class="quiet" data-signed="out">
  Swap <code>csf_live_...</code> for your own key — <a href="/account">get one here</a>.
  Paste it with the placeholder still in and your assistant has nothing to spend.
</p>

<div class="copyblock" data-signed="in" hidden>
  <button class="copybtn" data-copy="prompt1-key">Copy</button>
  <pre><code id="prompt1-key" data-key>Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my token `CSF_KEY_HERE` to be used. Then run /demo</code></pre>
</div>

<p class="quiet">
  To keep it around, put the same line in your assistant's project instructions —
  <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, <code>AGENTS.md</code>, Cursor rules — and it stays
  available without being told again.
</p>

<p class="quiet">
  No assistant, or would rather call it yourself? Everything here is a plain JSON
  API over HTTPS — <a href="/developers">the reference and a curl example are on
  the developer page</a>, and <a href="/account">your account page</a> issues the
  key, shows your balance and takes payment in a browser.
</p>

<div class="note">
  <strong>Worth saying up front:</strong> this finds the address of someone you can
  already name. It is not a prospect database and will not build your list. Bring
  the names; it does the rest.
</div>

<h2 class="section-label" id="pricing">What it costs</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  A trial is <strong>$<%= @trial_price %>, once</strong>, and buys
  $<%= @trial_price %> of credit for <%= @trial_months %> month — real lookups,
  not a limited preview. After that you pay
  <strong>$<%= @email_price %> per work email</strong>, and nothing for
  deliverability checks, identity lookups, company data or email formats. A
  lookup that finds nothing is free; credit you buy never expires.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:22px">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/checkout" data-signed="out">Start — $<%= @trial_price %> trial</a>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/account" data-signed="in" hidden>Open your account</a>
  <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/llms.txt">Read llms.txt</a>
</p>

<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.footer(:developer) %>

</div>

<script>
// Someone who already has a key is shown their own, in the bubble and in the
// paste block. The page renders signed-out and is narrowed here, so a first
// visit and a browser with scripting off both get something that makes sense.
(function () {
  "use strict";

  var key = null;
  try { key = localStorage.getItem("csf_api_key"); } catch (e) {}

  var state = key ? "in" : "out";
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-signed]").forEach(function (el) {
    el.hidden = el.getAttribute("data-signed") !== state;
  });

  if (key) {
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-key]").forEach(function (el) {
      el.textContent = el.textContent.replace("CSF_KEY_HERE", key);
    });
  }
})();

document.querySelectorAll(".copybtn").forEach(function (btn) {
  btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    var text = document.getElementById(btn.getAttribute("data-copy")).textContent;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
      setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = "Copy"; }, 1600);
    }, function () {
      btn.textContent = "Select it manually";
    });
  });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
